From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:18:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: sleep: Add
 apple,spmi-extra-bus

Some machines have an SPMI slave that their own OS puts to sleep at the
commit but that has no node in the tree, on a bus with no debug port
controller. Let the sleep node name that bus so the driver can reach
the slave.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml   | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
index 7d82a92d6d..543ec48aa5 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
@@ -80,6 +80,13 @@ properties:
     description:
       The USB-C port controller that carries the debug link, stopped for a sleep.
 
+  apple,spmi-extra-bus:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      An SPMI controller that has a slave the machine's own OS puts to sleep
+      at the commit but no node in this tree, for a machine whose debug
+      port is not on SPMI. Nothing is sent to it unless a slave is named.
+
   apple,display-coprocessors:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
     description:
-- 
2.43.0

